{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Like drought in Zion.</b> Like in a land of drought (Jeremiah 2:6)." "<b>The noise of strangers You humble.</b> Now 'drought in the shadow of a cloud' is duplicated in meaning." "Now <b>in the shadow of a cloud</b> is when the cloud is hidden and is not seen." "Now <b>the song of tyrants</b> is like 'the noise of strangers,' from the root of songs (Isaiah 24:16)." "<b>He humbles.</b> From the root עני (poor), and it is an intransitive verb, and from the root לענות מפני (Exodus 6:3)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:05.352456394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}